      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Organic debris in Adzerak’s ruined corridor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A one-inch, maggot-like grub found in refuse."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Special attacks and weaknesses mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Burrow into exposed flesh · A grub has a percentage chance equal to the target’s base AC to burrow into exposed flesh. The encounter gives no THAC0 or standard attack or damage. If untreated, the grubs reach the heart and kill the victim in 1d3 turns.",
            "Fire and cure disease · Fire kills 2d10 grubs if applied before 1d6 rounds of burrowing. A cure disease spell kills all the grubs outright."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Ruined corridor · While characters search or handle the rubbish in area 12, there is a cumulative 10% chance per turn of an encounter. Each such encounter has an equal chance of being ten Rot Grubs or fifty Pernicons."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "10 appearing in this encounter. 1 HP and 15 XP per individual. Unsteady (5) morale. Nonintelligent (0). Neutral.",
            "John Terra, Four from Cormyr (TSR, 1997), The Bibliophile, area 12, p. 16."
          ]
        }
