          "sections": [
            {
              "title": "Classification",
              "lines": [
                "Medium Swarm of Tiny Beasts, unaligned"
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Other statistics",
              "lines": [
                "Resists piercing and slashing. Immune to Charmed, Frightened, Grappled, Paralyzed, Petrified, Prone and Restrained. Blindsight 10 ft., passive Perception 6. No languages."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Traits",
              "lines": [
                "Swarm. It can share a space with creatures and fit through an opening that admits a Tiny maggot. It cannot regain HP or gain temporary HP."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Actions",
              "lines": [
                "Bites. Melee weapon attack +0, reach 0 ft., one creature sharing its space. On a hit, 1d4 grubs infest the creature. At the start of each of its turns it takes 1d6 piercing per grub. Before the end of the creature’s next turn, fire applied to the wound inflicts 1 fire damage and kills those grubs. After that they have burrowed too far for fire. Disease-curing effects kill all infesting grubs. An infested creature that ends its turn at 0 HP dies."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Encounter context",
              "lines": [
                "Single rot grub. On contact, a DC 10 Dexterity save avoids infestation. On a failure, use the swarm’s infestation rules for one grub, including 3 (1d6) piercing damage at the start of each host turn. Burning an infested corpse kills the grubs inside."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Habitats",
              "lines": [
                "Underdark and swamps, especially corpses and decaying material."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Appearance",
              "lines": [
                "A mass of finger-sized maggots that burrow into flesh."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Table notes",
              "lines": [
                "Rules source: Volo's Guide to Monsters, p. 208."
              ]
            }
